    "summary_one_sentence": "An elderly widow working night shifts at a coastal aquarium forms a heartwarming bond with a remarkably clever octopus, leading her to uncover a life-changing truth about her past.",
    "summary_short": "Tova Sullivan, a 70-year-old widow coping with loss and the unsolved disappearance of her son decades ago, finds solace in her nightly cleaning job at the Sowell Bay Aquarium. She forms an unlikely friendship with Marcellus, a remarkably intelligent Giant Pacific octopus with a habit of sneaking out of his tank. When an injury forces Tova to take time off, a young drifter named Cameron arrives as her temporary replacement. Guided by Marcellus's surprisingly perceptive instincts, Tova and Cameron uncover a shared past that brings healing, truth, and unexpected family connection.",
    "summary_long": "Following the deaths of her husband and her 18-year-old son Erik decades earlier, Tova Sullivan maintains order in her life through routine, taking a job as a night cleaner at the local Sowell Bay Aquarium. During her quiet shifts, she strikes up an extraordinary relationship with Marcellus, an extraordinarily intelligent Giant Pacific octopus nearing the end of his lifespan. After Tova saves Marcellus during one of his sneaky nighttime escapes, she injures her ankle and must temporarily step away from her duties. Cameron Cassmore, a directionless 30-year-old searching for his estranged biological father, takes over Tova's shift at the aquarium. Tova guides Cameron on taking pride in his work, and the two form a warm mentor-mentee bond. Meanwhile, Marcellus detects a profound connection between Tova and Cameron using discarded clues and personal items. Frustrated by dead ends in his search, Cameron hurls a class ring belonging to his father into an aquarium tank, which Marcellus retrieves. Before passing away, Marcellus helps deliver the ring to Tova, who recognizes the initials as belonging to her late son Erik. Realizing Cameron is her long-lost grandson, Tova finds closure for her grief and embraces a hopeful future alongside her newfound family.",
    "synopsis": "Set in the misty Pacific Northwest coastal town of Sowell Bay, 'Remarkably Bright Creatures' follows Tova Sullivan, a reserved 70-year-old widow who turns to a night-shift cleaning job at the local aquarium to cope with unresolved grief. Decades after the unexplained disappearance of her teenage son and the more recent loss of her husband, Tova finds unexpected comfort in the company of Marcellus, a remarkably clever Giant Pacific octopus who observes human behavior from his glass enclosure. When Tova's life crosses paths with Cameron, a struggling young man who arrives in town seeking answers about his own past, an unlikely intergenerational friendship forms. Through shared routines, community bonds, and the subtle interventions of a remarkably perceptive marine creature, the characters embark on a heartwarming journey toward healing, forgiveness, and second chances.",
